course: religion-ethics
lesson: 11
title: Psalms and Proverbs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The Book of Psalms is the Bible's song book: 150 songs and prayers, many linked with King David, still sung and prayed by Jews and Christians today.
explain: The Psalms hold every feeling — joy and thanks (Psalm 100), trust (Psalm 23, Psalm 46), wonder at being known (Psalm 139), and sad or angry cries of «How long, O Lord?» (Psalm 13).
explain: So the Psalms teach a child that you can bring anything to God, even fear or anger, and that honest prayer is not rude prayer.
explain: The Book of Proverbs is a collection of short wise sayings, many linked with King Solomon, about everyday life: how we speak, how we work, whom we choose as friends.
explain: «A gentle answer turns away wrath» is advice for the playground today: a calm word can stop a fight that a harsh word would start.
fact: The Book of Psalms has 150 psalms, which are songs and prayers used in worship by Jews and Christians.
fact: Many psalms are linked with King David, who was a shepherd boy before he became king.
fact: Psalm 23 begins «The Lord is my shepherd» and pictures God leading, feeding and protecting, even through the darkest valley.
fact: Psalm 23 is often read at funerals because Christians find comfort in it that God is with them in hard times.
fact: Psalm 100 calls all the earth to «make a joyful noise» and to worship God with gladness and thanks.
fact: Psalm 139 says that God knows each person completely and that we are «fearfully and wonderfully made».
fact: Psalm 46 says «God is our refuge and strength» and «Be still, and know that I am God».
fact: Psalms of lament are prayers of sorrow or complaint, such as Psalm 13, which asks «How long, O Lord?».
fact: The Book of Proverbs is a collection of short wise sayings, many linked with King Solomon.
fact: Proverbs 15:1 says «A gentle answer turns away wrath, but a harsh word stirs up anger».
fact: Proverbs 6:6 says «Go to the ant, you sluggard; consider its ways and be wise» (a sluggard is a lazy person), praising steady hard work and planning.
fact: Proverbs 16:18 says «Pride goes before destruction, a haughty spirit before a fall».
fact: Proverbs 13:20 says «Walk with the wise and become wise», because the friends we choose shape who we become.
exercise: How many psalms are there in the Book of Psalms? | 150 | 12 | 40 | 365
exercise: Which king are many of the psalms linked with? | King David | King Herod | King Solomon only | King Saul
exercise: What are the psalms? | Songs and prayers used in worship | Short laws about food and washing | Letters written to the first churches | Stories about the life of Jesus
exercise: In Psalm 23, what picture is used for God? | A shepherd caring for his sheep | A king sitting on a high throne | A builder laying strong foundations | A farmer sowing seed in a field
exercise: Why is Psalm 23 often read at funerals? | It comforts people that God is with them in dark times | It is the shortest psalm in the whole Bible, so it is quick to read | It tells the story of a funeral long ago | It was written for a king's funeral only
exercise: What does Psalm 100 call all the earth to do? | Make a joyful noise and worship God with thanks | Keep silent and stay still before God | Build a temple in the city of Jerusalem | Fast for forty days in the desert
exercise: What does Psalm 139 say about each person? | God knows them completely and made them wonderfully | God only notices the people who pray every single day | God forgets about people completely when they do wrong | God knows only kings, priests and prophets by their names
exercise: Which line comes from Psalm 46? | Be still, and know that I am God | The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not want | Make a joyful noise unto the Lord | Go to the ant, you sluggard
exercise: What is a psalm of lament? | A prayer telling God of sorrow or complaint | A happy song that is sung only at big weddings | A list of wise sayings about work and money | A prayer that is forbidden to be said out loud
exercise: Why do Christians think it is right that the Psalms include sad and angry prayers? | It shows we can be honest with God about every feeling | It shows the writers had stopped believing in God | It warns us never to feel sad or angry | It proves that God only hears happy prayers
exercise: What is the Book of Proverbs? | A collection of short wise sayings for everyday life | A book of songs for the Temple choir | The story of how the world was made | A record of the kings of Israel and all of their wars
exercise: «A gentle answer turns away wrath» means… | A calm reply can stop anger growing | You should never answer anyone at all | Gentle people always win every argument | Angry people should be ignored forever
exercise: Why does Proverbs tell the lazy person to look at the ant? | The ant works steadily and plans ahead | The ant is the strongest of all creatures | The ant never needs to eat or rest | The ant always works alone without help
exercise: What does «Pride goes before a fall» warn about? | Boasting and arrogance set us up to fail | Climbing high places is always forbidden | Proud people are always the best at things | Falling over is a punishment from God
exercise: «Walk with the wise and become wise» is advice about… | Choosing our friends well | Going on long walks each day | Studying alone without friends | Obeying the king in everything
exercise: Which king are many of the Proverbs linked with? | King Solomon | King Ahab | King Herod | King Pharaoh of Egypt
test: my sister says psalms are just the boring bits u skip in church. what r they actually | Songs and prayers, many still sung in worship today | Old laws nobody follows any more | Stories about Jesus' miracles | Rules for priests in the Temple
test: Josh: «Psalm 23 says God is like a king on a throne.» Put him right. | It pictures God as a shepherd who leads and protects | It pictures God as a soldier who fights wars for his people | It pictures God as a judge in a court | It pictures God as a fisherman with a net
test: A classmate who does not believe in God asks why Christians read Psalm 23 at funerals. Best answer? | It comforts them that God stays with them in the darkest times | It is a rule in the Bible that every single funeral has to use it | It explains exactly what heaven looks like | It is the only psalm people still know
test: im so angry at God my nan died. is it wrong to say that in a prayer | No, the Psalms show people telling God honestly of sorrow and anger | Yes, God only listens to thankful and happy prayers | Yes, angry prayers are banned in the Bible | No, because God does not hear prayers at all
test: kid at lunch: «shut up or i'll smash ur face». which reply fits Proverbs 15:1 | A calm, gentle word that does not throw it back | A harsher threat back so that he backs right off | Laughing at him loudly in front of everyone there | Calling him names right back until he starts to cry
test: «God only cares about important people» — which psalm says otherwise? | Psalm 139, which says God knows each person completely | Psalm 100, which says only kings may worship | Psalm 46, which says God is far away | Psalm 13, which says God has forgotten everyone for good
test: Mia left her olympiad revision till the night before — «sod it, I'll wing it». Which proverb speaks to her? | Go to the ant: work steadily and plan ahead | A gentle answer turns away wrath | Be still, and know that I am God | The Lord is my shepherd, I shall not want
test: Ben boasted he'd win the race without training, then came last. Which saying fits? | Pride goes before a fall | Make a joyful noise to the Lord | Walk with the wise and become wise | How long, O Lord?
test: mum says «walk with the wise» cos my new mates keep getting detentions. what does she mean | The friends we choose shape who we become | We should walk to school instead of driving | Only clever people are allowed friends | We must never talk to anyone in detention
test: Judge: «Psalms are prayers to God; Proverbs are mostly what?» | Practical wise sayings about everyday life | Prayers of sorrow and of complaint sung to God | Prophecies about what will happen in the future | Commandments that were given on Mount Sinai
test: Before a big exam you feel panicky. Which psalm line is about calm trust? | Be still, and know that I am God | Go to the ant, you sluggard | Pride goes before a fall | Walk with the wise and become wise
exam: Ascertain the number of compositions contained within the Book of Psalms. | One hundred and fifty | Twelve | Forty | Three hundred and sixty-five
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the inclusion of psalms of lament within the Psalter? | They demonstrate that sorrow and complaint may be honestly addressed to God | They demonstrate that the authors had abandoned their faith | They demonstrate that sorrow is prohibited to believers | They demonstrate that God attends solely to praise
exam: Identify the principal teaching conveyed by the maxim «A gentle answer turneth away wrath». | That a mild reply tends to diminish anger | That no reply ought ever to be given | That the meek invariably prevail in disputes | That anger ought to be met with silence forever
exam: It is given that a pupil is counselled to «walk with the wise». Select the response consistent with the intent of the said counsel. | One's choice of companions shapes one's character | One ought to undertake daily walks for the sake of one's health | One ought to associate solely with scholars | One ought to avoid all company entirely
